.SH NAME
maknoon-identity-publish - Anchor your active identity to a registry (Nostr, WKD, or DNS)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaknoon identity publish [handle] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Publishes your identity (ML-KEM + ML-DSA public keys) to one or more registries
so that other Maknoon users can encrypt directly to you by handle.

.PP
Registries:
  --nostr     Publish to Nostr relays (default). No infrastructure required.
              Recipients resolve you via @handle or user@domain.com (NIP-05).
  --wkd       Web Key Directory — place a JSON file on your own HTTPS server at
              https:///.well-known/maknoon/\&.json
              Works for alice@example.com handles. No DNS changes required.
  --dns       Generate a DNS TXT record (_maknoon.) for manual setup.
  --desec     Auto-publish the DNS record via deSEC.io API.
  --local     Pin to local contacts only (no network publishing).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--desec\fP[=false]
	Auto-publish DNS record via deSEC.io (requires --desec-token or DESEC_TOKEN)

.PP
\fB--desec-token\fP=""
	deSEC.io API token

.PP
\fB--dns\fP[=false]
	Generate a _maknoon DNS TXT record (manual setup)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for publish

.PP
\fB--local\fP[=false]
	Pin identity to local contacts only (no network)

.PP
\fB--nostr\fP[=false]
	Publish to Nostr relays (default when no other registry is specified)

.PP
\fB--wkd\fP[=false]
	Web Key Directory: publish as an HTTPS static file (requires alice@domain.com handle)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
